      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Argath, Bastion of Illdaera [zone=806]\n**Who:**\n- Atleris, Council Pinnacle [ _Quests, Missions, Raid_]\nRating:\n0/4**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 4 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 05:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Box of Craet Sprigs [item=100037]\n- Craet Scythe [item=97985]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Akesli Temlo [npc=38117]\n- Arthik Jantis [npc=38121]\n- Hauler Dinalo [npc=38118]\n- Lanessic Elset [npc=38125]\n- Magistrate Altara [npc=38116]\n- Mechanic Dalaber [npc=38122]\n- Noble Allingvy [npc=38119]\n- Record Keeper Talantia [npc=38120]\n- Troopwielder Balath [npc=38123]\n- Troopwielder Baris [ _Quest_]\n- Troopwielder Latakan [npc=38126]\n- a craet looter [npc=38127]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Argath #2: Shoring Up Defenses [quest=5389]\n- Argath #3: Protect the Arms [quest=5412]\n- Argath #4: The Riddle of Steel [quest=5413]\n- Argath #5: Breaking Ballistae [quest=5414]\n- Argath #6: Critical Mass [quest=5415]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 15 16:29:29 2011\nModified: Thu Jan 30 08:24:15 2025 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is the first task in a series of six; a solo task that begins with Atleris, Council Pinnacle, in Argath. He's located in the council building at -10, 445, 3 (west-central part of the zone-in area)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Atleris, Council Pinnacle'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle looks at you with resignation. 'It has come to this. Argath was once the pinnacle of strength in Alaris. A single warrior could cleave the helms of a hundred Erillion Blades. A regiment would secure surrender from a city with the mere whisper of our advance. Our mountain bled the finest steel; our steel bled our foes of life. Might and skill were ours, and we [lived] for battle.\nYou say, 'Lived?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says ''Indeed, so we once lived. But all things die. As from the corpses of wild and savage beasts grows the grass, warriors become crafters, swords become spades, and spears become cogs and gears. Peace has a way of conquering the strongest soldiers. Calm centuries dimmed the light of battle in our hearts. Commerce became our commander, and it dispatched us to the corners of Alaris, bearing [life] instead of death.'\nYou say, 'Life?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'The treaty with Erillion ended our lives as warriors. With the land at peace, we were reborn. We built houses, buttressed temples, and harvested crops. With our steel, we crafted the implements of Alaris, everything from walking sticks to sky ships. Our might strengthened others, while our own power withered. Now it has come to this: Argath needs the [help] of [outsiders].'\nYou say, 'Outsiders, us?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'What are you? Arriving on ships that rival the fleets of Windsong, you stride through our city with bold countenance, speaking as though unafraid of any Argathian or Erillian. Your shapes and sizes are varied and perplexing. You carry weapons of which even our Forge attendants could not conceive. You bring with you the smell of [battle]; I know you have taken many lives and would not hesitate to do so again.'\nYou say, 'What battle?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'I barely recognize it. You see these robes I wear. I have never lifted a sword. Time and peace made us weak, and most of us cannot handle a blade. Only the Regiment knows of battle, but they are tyros. Let it not be said outside this chamber, but Erillion will overwhelm us; our [defenses] will collapse.'\nYou say, 'Defenses?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'Many nights have passed since Erillion breached the gates. Our citizens cower on higher ground, while the Regiment stymies the enemy with arrows. Our supplies dwindle; our defenders are slain. Argath will not last. You are our only recourse. Will you [help] us?'\nYou say, 'I'll help!'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'If we must, we shall employ your kind as mercenaries. Erillion must be driven from Argath. Our Forge, our livelihood, must be protected. Speak with Magistrate Altara; al coordinates the mercenary outsiders. Go now. Argath must not fall, or Erillion will rule Alaris. '\nYou have been assigned the task 'This Is Argath'.\nThe fortress of Argath has been besieged by the forces of Erilliion. Atleris, Pinnacle of Argath's council, has been using the newly arrived Norrathians to prevent Erillion from conquering all of Argath. Now, Atleris asks you to do what you can to aid the Argathians' defense.\nMagistrate Altara, residing within the Pinnacle of Argath, coordinates the efforts of the many Norrathians in Argath.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Magistrate Altara 0/1 (Argath)\n_Altara is found in the room to the south of the council chamber (-90, 400, 8)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Magistrate Altara'\nMagistrate Altara says 'Another one of you? There must be many cities in the lands beyond the mists. It astonishes me how many strange creatures I have seen stepping from the ships on the dock, and they all seem so eager to help. Of course, some of our Champions have had to deal with unruly outsiders who want to test their strength against Argathians. But you are not like those fools, are you? No, or else [Atleris] would not have sent you to me.'\nYou say, 'Atleris'\nMagistrate Altara says 'The invasion weighs heavily on the Pinnacle of the Council. Alir mood can be dark at times. I do not share alir pessimism, though. The outsiders have brought me new hope that Argath is not lost. When the first of you began arriving, Atleris ordered our spellwielders to destroy your ships. al thought your presence was a ploy of Erillion or Windsong. Were it not for my protestations, many of you would be dead. Because of my advocacy for the outsiders, I am their [coordinator].'\nYou say, 'Their coordinator?'\nMagistrate Altara says 'Given Erillion besieges us, and we have only the food we grow here on the Crown, I cannot allow outsiders to run around Argath with no direction. I [direct] their efforts, making certain we work toward the defeat of Erillion and maintain our food supply.'\nYou say, 'How do you direct the efforts?'\nMagistrate Altara says 'I have met enough outsiders to know not all of them can handle a blade. Some should lead peaceful lives as craftsmen or farmers. I can see you are eager to fight Erillion, but I judge you would be better suited helping the haulers [deliver] craet grain.'\nYou say, 'Helping deliver craet?'\nMagistrate Altara says 'Many of our haulers have been killed delivering supplies to the Forge Overlook. The enemy camped in the Belly of Argath fires onto the Breath Spiral and the Overlook, catching our haulers as they unload their cargo. With so many dead, we must turn to outsiders to do their [jobs].'\nYou say, 'What jobs?'\nMagistrate Altara says 'We need to deliver grain to everyone in Argath. This will give you a chance to prove your usefulness to us, and to see our city. Speak with Akesli Temlo. I believe al has almost finished harvesting a bundle of craet. Al will tell you where it needs to go.'\nSpeak with Akesli Temlo 0/1 (Argath)\n_Task Window Says:_ Akesli Temlo gathers grain from the small farm atop Argath's Crown. Altara wants you to assist with the harvest.\n_Akesli Temlo is found southeast of the council building, across the stream (-260, 100, 2)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Akesli Temlo'\nAkesli Temlo says 'Greetings, outsider. I will have to thank Altara for sending you to me! I was just about to finish harvesting a bundle of craet grain, but I could always use your help. Here, take this scythe and finish cutting the remaining sprigs I need.'\n_You receive a Craet Scythe._\nHarvest 8 sprigs of craet grain 0/8 (Argath)\n_Task Window Says:_ Akesli needs only a few more sprigs of grain. Use the scythe al gave you to finish the harvest.\n_You can stand in the plantation nearby and right-click the scythe (you'll occasionally fail) until you get eight updates._\nSpeak with Akesli Temlo 0/1 (Argath)\n_Task Window Says:_ Ask Akesli what you need to do with the grain.\nYou say, 'Hail, Akesli Temlo'\nAkesli Temlo says 'You work quickly! I wish I had five more outsiders like you to tend these fields! You wouldn't know much less about craet grain than I. We planted this farm only weeks ago, after the Forge incident and Erillion's overtures of war. We feared our food supply from the Valley of Lunanyn would be cut off, so the farmers of Lunanyn gave us craet. The farmers would know better than I how to properly plant and harvest it. But you do not have time to listen to me. You should deliver these sprigs to the people of Argath. Hauler Dinalo will help you bundle the craet.'\nSpeak with Hauler Dinalo 0/1 (Argath)\n_Hauler Dinalo is found next to Akesli._\nYou say, 'Hail, Hauler Dinalo'\nYou receive a box of craet sprigs.\nHauler Dinalo says 'Altara has outsiders working as haulers now? It is shameful we cannot manage the task ourselves. Far longer than I have lived, haulers have been carrying goods from one end of Alaris to another. Now we cannot even carry a bundle of craet in our own [city].'\nYou say, 'Your city?'\nHauler Dinalo says 'As you no doubt have heard, Erillion has besieged Argath. When we try to deliver supplies to our defenders at the Forge Overlook, Erillian archers aim for our heads. Many of us have been [killed]. If this were not bad enough, hunger has driven some Argathians to thievery, raiding our storehouses and depleting our resources. Other Argathians have turned traitorous, attacking our own soldiers in the name of Erillion, hoping to be spared from execution if Erillion conquers Argath.'\nYou say, 'Killed?'\nHauler Dinalo says 'Do not worry, though. I will not send you right away to the Forge Overlook. Here is your list of Argathians to whom you should deliver craet sprigs. I have prepared the bundle. It is a bit heavy. Drag it if you must. Good luck, and watch for arrows!'\nHail Noble Allingvi 0/1 (Argath)\n_If you look at your map, there are four small buildings on the inside of the river. Noble Allingvi is in the northeast building (location 80, -75, 5)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Noble Allingvy'\nNoble Allingvy says 'Ah, my craet sprigs! Rations have diminished since the last delivery. Have you been eating my sprigs? No matter; it is either you or some other outsider siphoning food from the mouths of Argathians. I do not know why Atleris has tolerated your presence. Erillion still controls the Belly of Argath, in more ways than one. The outsiders have not [helped] in the least!'\nYou say, 'Helped?'\nNoble Allingvy says 'Yes, you did bring my craet sprigs. Thank you. But I would have you working on the truly useful things: driving off Erillion and giving me back my [home]!'\nYou say, 'Home?'\nNoble Allingvy says 'After the Forge incident, survivors were relocated to the Arms, the Neck, and the Crown. Atleris ordered us nobles to give up some of our houses to shelter affected Argathians. Then Erillion invaded, and more citizens were moved from the Arms to the higher reaches of Argath. Many nobles had to leave homes altogether and find residence in the palace. And so here I am.'\nHail Record Keeper Talantia 0/1 (Argath)\n_Record Keeper Talantia is found in the room north of the council chamber (120, 525, 8)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Record Keeper Talantia'\nRecord Keeper Talantia says 'Thank you, outsider. I know you are busy, but will you [speak] with me a moment?'\nYou say, 'I'll speak with you'\nRecord Keeper Talantia says 'The tomes hold no record of your kind. Since the arrival of outsiders, I have scoured our annals in search of some description matching what has been arriving on our dock. But in all history, no Argathian has seen or heard of beings beyond the [Alaris] mists.'\nYou say, 'The Alaris mists?'\nRecord Keeper Talantia says 'We thought we were a people alone in this solitary land. Argath, Sarith, Windsong, Alra, and Erillion have been our centers of civilization as far back as our lore exists. The only exception is the founding of our city, but that is only a [legend].'\nYou say, 'A legend?'\nRecord Keeper Talantia says 'The namesake of our city, Illdaera, was said to be a powerful warrior who sought to craft the mightiest blade in the land. Al searched far and wide for the best source of iron, commanding alir soldiers to dig in every place they camped. Al would conquer cities to dig beneath them and search for iron; al could leave no part of Alaris unsearched. Then al found the mountain of [Argath].'\nYou say, 'Argath?'\nRecord Keeper Talantia says 'When the soldiers dug into the mountain, gouts of molten metal surged to the surface, killing many soldiers. Illdaera knew it was not ordinary iron, and al ordered a sword be forged from the metal. Drawing the sword from a pail of water, al swung it at a rock above the oozing wound of the mountain, cleaving it in twain. This was not iron; this was the most fantastic [steel] in all of Alaris.'\nYou say, 'What steel?'\nRecord Keeper Talantia says 'It was light as bronze but harder than stone. Illdaera wielded the sword and cut alir way into the mountain, piercing its heart. Around the wound, al built the Forge, the source of Argath's power. Armed with the mightiest blade in Alaris, crafted from the mightiest steel, Illdaera raised the city of Argath, a bastion which no adversary could [overtake].'\nYou say, 'Overtake?'\nRecord Keeper Talantia says 'Erillion certainly has proven the legend false. And with your appearance, I do not know what is true anymore. But I have kept you long enough. I will let you return to your deliveries.'\nHail Arthik Jantis 0/1 (Argath)\n_Arthik is found in the southernmost building on the crown (-265, 0, 5)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Arthik Jantis'\nArthik Jantis says 'Craet! I thought I would never see it again! Citizens do not get a taste until everyone in the palace chews on it first. And you probably chewed on it too. Back when I lived on the Arms, craet was plentiful, and my belly was always full. After the Council [relocated] us, though, I have been getting leaner.'\nYou say, 'Relocated?'\nArthik Jantis says 'After the Forge incident, I had to leave my home and my shop, making room for the displaced citizens from the Belly. I settled in the Neck for a while, but then Erillion invaded, and we were all shifted higher. Now, here I am, still hungry. Have any more grain?'\nHail Mechanic Dalaber 0/1 (Argath)\n_Head southeast to the ledge (-385, -170, -12)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Mechanic Dalaber'\nMechanic Dalaber says 'This is all you have? I am about to send down a shipment, but there is not enough here to sustain the Regiment. Even outsiders make poor haulers! We [mechanics] merely control the machines. Haulers must bring the right amount of goods!'\nYou say, 'Mechanics?'\nMechanic Dalaber says 'We keep Argath running. I personally built this crane, and I maintain it. We craft the machines that built Alaris! What have you done, hauler? You brought the stones; I built the palace!'\nHail Troopwielder Baris 0/1 (Argath)\n_Troopwielder Baris is up on the ledge at -235, -235, 12._\nYou say, 'Hail, Troopwielder Baris'\nTroopwielder Baris says 'Altara has you hauling craet? What a waste! I have seen the power outsiders wield. If we had an army of them, we would crush the invaders and drive them back to Erillion. The enemy has not encroached upon the Crown, so you are not needed yet among my troops. If I were stationed on the [Overlook], though, I would hand you a bow and put you in my lines of archers. Though we are [inexperienced], I have no doubt your skill would more than compensate.'\nYou say, 'The Overlook?'\nTroopwielder Baris says 'Where Argath's Arms meet, directly above the Forge. Illdaera's Breath cascades through the Breath Spiral of the Neck, spilling onto the Forge Overlook before finally falling into the cooling molds outside the Forge. If you are traveling to the Overlook, be cautious. Erillion fires constantly upon the Neck and Overlook. Many haulers have died delivering supplies to troops and refugees.'\nYou say, 'Why are you inexperienced?'\nTroopwielder Baris says 'Argath long ago abandoned war. The Council maintained the Regiment as a small strike force, capable of mobilizing for brief campaigns beyond Argath. With Alaris at peace, we had no need for a larger army. And with Argath's [impenetrable] walls, the city was its own defense.'\nYou say, 'Impenetrable?'\nTroopwielder Baris says 'Were it not for the [incident] at the Forge, Erillion would never have entered our city.'\nYou say, 'What incident?'\nTroopwielder Baris says 'The eruption. The Forge boiled over. Rivers of steel poured into the Belly, flooding homes and workshops in fire, weakening the walls of Argath, lowering our guard. Erillion attacked days later.'\nHail Lanessic Elset 0/1 (Argath)\n_Head due north from the Troopwielder to the steps down at 85, -220, 12. Go to the second level down (z-loc -145) and into the first room on your right (loc -95, -160, -149)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Lanessic Elset'\nLanessic Elset says 'You are not hurt, are you? We do not see many haulers. Most of them lie dead at the bottom of the Spiral, killed by Erillian archers or magicians. Few of us venture outside anymore. It would have been better to remain in [Lunanyn] than escape to a prison in these cliffs.'\nYou say, 'Lunanyn?'\nLanessic Elset says 'Erillion claimed the valley beneath Argath. We farmers of the valley once provided food for much of Alaris, including Argath and Erillion. When Erillian troops marched upon us, we fled to Argath. Generiously, the Argathians gave us these homes in the Neck. But now this generosity is more of a curse. I am sure I will die either of an arrow or hunger.'\nHail Troopwielder Balath 0/1 (Argath)\n_Back out of the room, all the way down the ramp, then due east to the Overlook (10, -495, -272)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Troopwielder Balath'\nTroopwielder Balath says 'An outsider hauler! No wonder you made it without a scratch! Craet sprigs, troops! If you are hungry, come get them. Never mind the [arrows]!'\nYou say, 'Arrows?'\nTroopwielder Balath says 'Erillion cannot hit anything directly above the Forge. We have the high ground, and the arches shield us. Besides, the enemy cannot move any closer with the [steel] still hot, so their aim is poor.'\nYou say, 'Steel?'\nTroopwielder Balath says 'That which allowed Erillion to invade has prevented them from taking the city. The steel lives! Around the flow, swords and spears have sprung to life, and globs of metal wander as if sentient. Erillion fears the steel and has not ventured to take the Forge or climb the arms. We sit here, [safe], until our food dwindles or the enemy becomes emboldened.'\nYou say, 'Safe?'\nTroopwielder Balath says 'Except for a few arrows, bolts, and magic blasts. But my troops never fear! My fellow troopwielders on the Arms might tell you differently, but they are mistaken. Argath will be victorious!'\nHail Troopwielder Latakan 0/1 (Argath)\n_Head north until you come to Latakan on a bridge at 860, -215, -270._\nYou say, 'Hail, Troopwielder Latakan'\nTroopwielder Latakan says 'You bear sprigs? And thieves have not accosted you? I do not want to accept your delivery while there are creat looters lurking nearby.'\nKill 2 looters or thieves 0/2 (Argath)\n_Task Window Says:_ It is too dangerous to hand over the grain when there are creat looters neaby. Defeat them.\n_Creat looters spawn to the west and south of Latakan. They hit for a max ~7,400._\nHail Troopwielder Latakan 0/1 (Argath)\n_Task Window Says:_ Now that the looters are dead, inform Troopwielder Latakan.\nYou say, 'Hail, Troopwielder Latakan'\nTroopwielder Latakan says 'You handled those thieves well, outsider. You should be fighting with the Regiment! Thieves and looters have run rampant on the arms. Ever since the invasion of Erillion and the evacuation of citizens to the Neck and Crown, thieves and looters have been searching for food and valuables in the abandoned workshops and storehouses. Some of these vile naeya have even turned traitorous, pledging loyalty to Erillion and working to sabotage Argath's defenses. We will soon make a push to destroy them. I could use you. First, though, you should return to Magistrate Altara and tell ali you have finished your duties.'\nSpeak with Magistrate Altara 0/1 (Argath)\nYou say, 'Hail, Magistrate Altara'\nMagistrate Altara says 'You were not killed, and you did not eat all the craet, judging from the size of your belly. I trust I can give you more responsibility. Troopwielder Baris told me al wanted to speak to an outsider about a pressing issue. Go to ali.'\n_Reward:_\n266 platinum\nExperience\nDecorative Stone Tablets\n- Decorative Stone Tablets [item=97977]",
