      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Argath, Bastion of Illdaera [zone=806]\n**Who:**\n- Atleris, Council Pinnacle [ _Quests, Missions, Raid_]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Airship Safety Suppression Device [item=100029]\n- Arm Cannon [item=100027]\n- Battle Orb [item=100028]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Argath: Reclaiming Argath [zone=818]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Aelsworth [npc=38254]\n- Magistrate Altara [npc=38253]\n- Mizzenblast [npc=38252]\n- a blazemage [npc=38497]\n- a blazemaster [npc=38499]\n- a deconstructor [npc=38496]\n- a demolisher [npc=38495]\n- a long range deathcaller [npc=38491]\n- a magic blast [npc=38501]\n- a salver [npc=38494]\n- a siege runner [npc=38503]\n- a tower archer [npc=38492]\n- an ornate chest - Reclaiming Argath [npc=38255]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Argath #1: This Is Argath [quest=5388]\n- Argath #2: Shoring Up Defenses [quest=5389]\n- Argath #3: Protect the Arms [quest=5412]\n- Argath #4: The Riddle of Steel [quest=5413]\n- Argath #6: Critical Mass [quest=5415]\n- Breaking Things Down [quest=4510]\n- Illdaera's Vengeance [quest=5417]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 16 02:06:55 2011\nModified: Sat Sep 14 08:20:32 2024 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis group mission begins with Atleris, Council Pinnacle in Argath, inside the council building on the zone-in level.\nPre-requisites for requesting the raid:\n\\- Completion of \"This is Argath\"\n\\- Completion of \"Shoring Up Defenses\"\n\\- Completion of \"Protect the Arms\"\n\\- Completion of \"The Riddle of Steel\"\n\\- Completion of \"Breaking Ballistae\"\n\\- Completion of \"Critical Mass\"\n\\- Minimum skill level in Alaran Language: 10\nYou say, 'Hail, Atleris, Council Pinnacle'\nYou say, 'I'll join you'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says '[Go] now. Mizzenblast waits by the dock.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Reclaiming Argath'.\nYou say, 'Ready to go!'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'Speak with Mizzenblast when you arrive.'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'May your actions save Argath!'\nIf you have completed the six pre-quest solo tasks but have not yet done this mission, you see this instead:\nYou say, 'Hail, Atleris, Council Pinnacle'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'Bursin lives? If you speak truthfully, the Forge will consume ali. I count all of the lost lives of those in the Forge; they have [sacrificed] themselves for Argath. But this is a weighty matter. We always need [help] delivering grain. You could again [speak] with Vitesal, if you wish to solve the mystery of the Forge. Or you could [work] with Alassin and Mizzenblast to defeat our enemies.'\nYou say, 'Sacrificed?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'The Forge will erupt. This can be delayed, not prevented. The Mountain will have its vengeance against Erillion. The enemy, and Argath with them, will drown in [steel].'\nYou say, 'Steel?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'The Mountain's steel ruined the Belly, and now Erillion occupies it. I would rather the whole of Argath sink into the heart of the mountain than see Erillion conquer my people. Either the Forge will [end] the lives of the enemy in the Belly, or I will.'\nYou say, 'End?'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'I conspired with the gnome, Mizzenblast. Alir weapons, unleashed upon the Belly, will devastate Erillion. The flying [ships] of the outsiders will swoop over the Belly and rain fire upon our enemies.'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'You would know best how to pilot your own ships. [Join] Mizzenblast, and wipe Erillion from Argath before the Mountain does!'\nYou say, 'I will join.'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says '[Go] now. Mizzenblast waits by the dock.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Reclaiming Argath'.\nYou say, 'Go.'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'Speak with Mizzenblast when you arrive.'\nAtleris, Council Pinnacle says 'May your actions save Argath!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Argath, Bastion of Illdaera.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Mizzenblast 0/1 (Argath)\nYou say, 'Hail, Mizzenblast'\nMizzenblast says 'Are you the only volunteers Atleris sent? I'm not surprised. The way he talks now, you'd think he would forfeit the lives of everyone in Argath just to defeat Erillion. And what are the lives of a few Norrathian [adventurers] compared to the lives of his own people?'\nYou say, 'Adventurers?'\nMizzenblast says 'I suppose risking your own life is the cost of exploring new lands and meeting new civilizations. We must choose sides when people are dying. Even though Atleris uses us for his own ends, his cause is just. I have seen enough of Argath to know I will do anything to [save] it.'\nYou say, 'Save?'\nMizzenblast says 'To do so, I have created my finest weapons yet: the Battle Orb and the Arm Cannon. The Battle Orb works using the same principle as my Exoblast: throw it in the midst of the enemy, and it will explode into shards of steel. The Arm Cannon functions like the LRK: aim it at your target and fire an armor-piercing projectile. With these weapons, and an [airship], you can't lose!'\nYou say, 'What airship?'\nMizzenblast says 'Aelsworth has been generous enough to lend us his airship for this mission -- well, generous enough to allow me to retrofit the ship with a more powerful steam engine once the [mission] is complete. There is a special feature you should know about this airship. It has a safety device that will bring you to the ship within five seconds if you fall off. There may be a situation where you need to disable this, and even go to the dock. For this, I will give you a device. If you hold the device in your dominant hand, it will keep the airship from protecting you, but only if you are at the dock. This device is powered by the airship, so will only work when it is around. The airship will also remove any corpses that are on it, and deposit them to the docks.'\nYou say, 'What mission?'\nMizzenblast says 'Take these Battle Orbs and Arm Cannons. I have given Arm Cannons only to those who have no magical abilities. It will allow you to attack your enemies at long range. The Battle Orbs I have given to everyone: when you are over the Belly, drop them on the Erillian troops. Now, ask Aelsworth about -- hold on! What is Magistrate Altara doing here?'\n_Everyone in the task receives a Battle Orb, an Arm Cannon, and an Airship Safety Suppression Device._\nSpeak with Magistrate Altara 0/1 (Argath)\nYou say, 'Hail, Magistrate Altara'\nMagistrate Altara says 'Outsider, Atleris sent me. You must know: Erillion and Windsong have taken our defensive towers that float beyond the fortress walls. With their new position, the enemy fires down upon the Arms and the Crown. And even now, Windsong flies more troops toward the Pinnacle. Before you can attack the troops in the Belly, you must [remove] the enemy from the towers!'\nYou say, 'Remove?'\nMagistrate Altara says 'You must hurry. Speak with Aelsworth and board the ship!'\nSpeak with Aelsworth 0/1 (Argath)\nYou say, 'Hail, Aelsworth'\nAelsworth says 'My ship isn't coming back in one piece, is it? I never should have made that deal with Mizzenblast...Oh, well, this is my only chance to get that new steam engine. Get on board before I change my mind!'\nBoard the airship 0/1 (Argath)\n_Everyone needs to get aboard the airship. NOTE: If you fall off at any time, you'll be ported back to its location. The ship will start moving on its own towards your first target._\nKill 6 invaders on the tower 0/6 (Argath)\n_Magistrate Altara emote:_ Kill the casters in the towers on your left!\nKill 6 invaders on the second tower 0/6 (Argath)\nKill 3 invaders that are attacking the Pinnacle 0/3 (Argath)\n_Magistrate Altara emote:_ Windsong attacks the Pinnacle!\nKill 3 invaders that are attacking the Pinnacle 0/3 (Argath)\nKill 6 blazemages on the third tower 0/6 (Argath)\n_For the above five steps, you need to use the Arm Cannons against the mobs (a click does 15k damage). They can also be damaged with regular ranged attacks (spells, archery, throwing)._\n_These mobs won't just stand there and be killed, however. They'll be using ranged attacks against you as well._\nFly toward the Belly 0/1 (Argath)\n_Magistrate Altara emote:_ Erillion has broken through defenses on the Arms! Kill them before they reach the top of the Spiral!\n_Once the first five kill steps are updated, you'll fly over the lower area (the ship will do this itself; you don't need to control it)._\nKill 8 siege runners 0/8 (Argath)\n_Target and attack the eight siege runners._\nEnter the Belly 0/1 (Argath)\n_Magistrate Altara emote:_ Fend off the magic blasts, and use the Battle Orbs to kill everything you can in the Belly!\n_Again, the ship will move into position on its own._\nDrop your Battle Orbs and kill the enemy below 0/15 (Argath)\n_Here, you need to target mobs below and click the Battle Orbs to drop bombs on them._\nKill 12 invaders on the final towers 0/12 (Argath)\n_Same as the first five kill steps -- Arm Cannons and ranged attacks._\nReturn to the dock 0/1 (Argath)\n_The ship will return on its own._\n_Aelsworth emote:_ No! My airship! What have you done to it?! Mizzenblast, you said everything would be fine!\n_Magistrate Altara emote:_ The Forge! It is erupting!\nSpeak with Magistrate Altara 0/1 (Argath)\nYou say, 'Hail, Magistrate Altara'\nMagistrate Altara says 'You have done well, but I am afraid our actions are too late to ward off the Mountain's anger. Take this reward for your efforts. Hopefully you will live long enough to get some use from it. [Go] to Atleris as soon as possible, though. We have not much time!'\nCollect your reward 0/1 (Argath)\n_NOTE: Make sure everyone is in range as the chest is opened. Anyone not in range won't get experience from the task._\n_Reward:_\nWell Worn Book\nExperience\n320 platinum\nPossible Chest Loot [npc=38255] (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task):\nClaws of the Bane\nFlanged Argathian Mace\nHusk Sharpened Axe\nMoonglow\nReviler's Steelwall\nSeal of the Reviler\nSpinestone of the Gravemaster\nTrinket of the Collector\nVeil of the Moon\nVelvet Drape of the Emissary\nMinor Alaran Cantrip\nLesser Alaran Cantrip\n- Well Worn Book [item=99364]",
    },
