      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Argath, Bastion of Illdaera [zone=806]\n**Who:**\n- General Tyronith [npc=38136]\nRating:\n0/2**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 2 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Erillion: The Order of Three [zone=838]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Arch Carnifex Wilo [npc=40039]\n- Beastmaster Graw [npc=40056]\n- Chief Official Pyntara [npc=40038]\n- General Tyronith [npc=40036]\n- Grand Archon Soliran [npc=40037]\n- High Priest Jerinos [npc=40040]\n- Illuminator Trellivino [npc=40057]\n- Tower of Light [npc=40042]\n- Tower of Strength [npc=40044]\n- Tower of the Skies [npc=40043]\n- Tower of the Tides [npc=40045]\n- Vocalist Oolamar [npc=40054]\n- Winly, Templar of Tides [npc=40055]\n- a bestial raptor [npc=40050]\n- a blazing braxi [npc=40052]\n- a bronze chest [npc=39459]\n- a dread light [npc=40053]\n- a jagged dervish [npc=40047]\n- a living mound [npc=40051]\n- a sharpshooter [npc=40041]\n- a tidal serpent [npc=40048]\n- a wastewater scavenger [npc=40049]\n- an infused selyrah [npc=40046]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Bronze #1: Dreams of Chaos [quest=5513]\n- Bronze #2: A Spy Among Us [quest=5514]\n- Bronze #3: Restoring Order [quest=5515]\n- Bronze #4: Political Favors [quest=5516]\n- Stop the Dreams [quest=5517]\n- The Traitor Revealed [quest=5519]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Dec 5 01:02:58 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n**NOTE: This is the quest entry for the group version of \"The Order of Three\". See this quest entry [quest=5545] for the raid version.**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with General Tyronith in Argath at approximately -25, 470, 9._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completed \"Dreams of Chaos\"\n\\- Completed \"A Spy Among Us\"\n\\- Completed \"Restoring Order\"\n\\- Completed \"Political Favors\"\n\\- Completed \"Stop the Dreams\"\n\\- Completed \"The Traitor Revealed\"\n\\- 81 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, General Tyronith'\nGeneral Tyronith says 'Hello, invader. I am hoping that you are the one that can help me. Some day we must defeat those that assault our city. If you can prove to me that you have the strength and the iron will, then I would like to send you to war with those of Erillion. Do you have the qualities that I seek? If so, will you along with a strong fighting force take on this [great task]? Even if your numbers are small, I can still use your [assistance].'\nYou say, 'You have my assistance'\nGeneral Tyronith says 'Good! I can see the steel in your heart. When you are ready we shall [go] into the heart of the city where our enemies dwell. Within the city walls are multiple towers fortified by magic, each kept aflame by a guardian who lingers close to their base. The first step to victory is to destroy those towers.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Order of Three'.\nThe citizens of the city have fled, inviting creatures to linger in the streets and allowing High Priest Jerinos absolute control. General Tyronith has asked for your help in reclaiming the City of Bronze.\nGeneral Tyronith will meet you outside the city gates with further instruction.\nYou say, 'Go'\nGeneral Tyronith says 'May Illdaera harden your heart and sharpen your mind.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Erillion, City of Bronze.\n\n---\n\n**Summary**\n_Once you hail General Tyronith inside the instanced zone, you'll have to make your way to the four corners of the city and, for each one, kill six creatures lurking about and then a named._\n_Throughout the task, the tower nearest you will randomly nuke you:_\n_Light:_\nLightbeam: Single Target, Fire (-800)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 24000\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 10000 per tick\n_Strength:_\nWeight of Steel: Single Target, Magic (-800)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 31000\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 5000 per tick\n3: Decrease Movement by 500%\n_Skies:_\nLightning Shock: Single Target, Magic (-800)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 5000\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 15000 per tick _(4 ticks)_\n_Tides:_\nWater Hammer: Single Target, Magic (-800)\n1: Stun (3.00 sec)\n2: Knockback (6) and Toss Up (4)\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 29000\n_After you've finished the towers, you'll make your way to the center of the city, outside the government building where you'll find High Priest Jerinos. Speak with Jerinos to trigger the last encounter._\n_You'll fight Grand Archon Soliran and then Jerinos will summon you to the rooftop. Fight Jerinos to approximately 70%, after which you'll be ported back down to fight Arch Carnifex Wilo. Once you're done with Wilo, you're back on the rooftop to fight Jerinos to approximately 40%. You'll then be ported back down to fight Chief Official Pyntara. Once Pyntara is dead, you'll be back on the rooftop to finish off Jerinos for the win._\n_NOTE: When you're ported from the ground to the rooftop, you have no opportunity for a rest. However, when you're ported from the rooftop to the ground, you can take time to rest as needed. The next mob you engage will not be in your aggro range, so you can pull it when you're ready._\n\n---\n\n**Speak with the General**\nSpeak with General Tyronith 0/1 (Erillion)\nYou say, 'Hail, General Tyronith'\nGeneral Tyronith says 'Your challenge lies within the city. If you feel the need, you may [leave] at any time; otherwise, we need to begin our offensive immediately. The citizens fled the city recently, or have hidden in their homes. This must be because they have summoned their allies, the priests of the other gods. They will have invested their power into those towers. You need to attract the attention of these priests, and then defeat them if you can. That should withdraw the power from most of the towers, weakening our enemies.'\n_Note: There is an achievement for completing this in the order presented (Skies, Tides, Strength, Light: Southeast, Southwest, Northeast, Northwest)._\n_Task Window Says:_ According to General Tyronith, destroying the towers that surround the city will weaken High Priest Jerinos' defenses. To get the tower keepers' attention however, you will need to slaughter creatures that wander the streets.\n\n---\n\n**The Towers: Skies**\nKill enemies near the Tower of Skies 0/6 (Erillion)\nDefeat Vocalist Oolamar to deactivate the Tower of Skies 0/1 (Erillion)\n_It's unknown if infused selyrahs cast any spells. Jagged dervishes cast \"Lightning Pulse\":_\nLightning Pulse: PB AE 50', Magic (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 30000\n_Upon killing the last of the six trash mobs, you'll see the emote:_\nVocalist Oolamar appears from within the Temple of the Skies.\n_Vocalist Oolamar spawns at the base of the tower. It casts \"Song for the Sea\" (increases incoming spell damage) and \"Resounding Denial\":_\nResounding Denial: Single Target, Chromatic (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 15000 per tick\n2: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect)\n3: Silence\n4: Increase Curse Counter by 12\nVocalist Oolamar has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nArch Carnifex Wilo cries out as the nearby towers grow still.\n\n---\n\n**The Towers: Tides**\nKill enemies near the Tower of Tides 0/6 (Erillion)\nDefeat Winly, Templar of Tides to deactivate the Tower of Tides 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Tidal serpents cast \"Liquification\"; wastewater scavengers cast \"Slippery Slime\" and \"Parasitic Infestation\":_\nLiquification: Single Target, Poison (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 19000 per tick _(3 ticks)_\n2: Decrease STR by 1000\n3: Decrease Movement by 100%\n4: Increase Poison Counter by 12\nSlippery Slime: PB AE 20', Unresistable (-940)\n1: Slow Push (70)\nParasitic Infestation: Single Target, Disease (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 8000 per tick\n2: Increase Disease Counter by 12\n3: Improved Spell Effect: Parasitic Explosion _(45k DD when it wears off)_\n_Upon killing the last of the six trash mobs, you'll see the emote:_\nWinly, Templar of Tides appears from within the Temple of Tides.\n_Winly casts \"Coat of Roiling Water\" (increases incoming spell damage) and \"Swirling Undertow\":_\nSwirling Undertow: PB AE 50', Cold (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 9000 per tick\n2: Decrease Movement by 50%\n3: Decrease Attack Speed by 50%\n4: Decrease Double Attack by 50%\n5: Increase Curse Counter by 12\nWinly, Templar of Tides has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nChief Official Pyntara cries out as the nearby towers grow still.\n\n---\n\n**The Towers: Strength**\nKill enemies near the Tower of Strength 0/6 (Erillion)\nDefeat Beastmaster Graw to deactivate the Tower of Strength 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Bestial raptors cast \"Thrash\" and \"Tail Thrash\"; living mounds cast \"Deadly Sprouts\":_\nTail Thrash: Directional 100', Unresistable (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 30000\n2: Knockback (2) and Toss Up (5)\nThrash: PB AE 40', Unresistable (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 30000\nDeadly Sprouts: Single Target, Poison (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 10000 per tick\n2: Increase Poison Counter by 12\n3: Improved Spell Effect: Sprouting Death _(2-tick 34K DOT + root if it wears off)_\n_Upon the last of the six kills, you see:_\nBeastmaster Graw appears from within the Tower of Strength.\n_Beastmaster Graw casts \"Coat of Oilflowers\" (increases incoming spell damage) and \"Kolos' Ravaging Teeth\":_\nKolos' Ravaging Teeth: PB AE 150', Magic (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 42000\n2: Fading Memories\n3: Stun (2.00 sec)\nBeastmaster Graw has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nGrand Archon Soliran cries out as the nearby towers grow still.\n\n---\n\n**The Towers: Light**\nKill enemies near the Tower of Light 0/6 (Erillion)\nDefeat Illuminator Trellivino to deactivate the Tower of Light 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Dread lights cast \"Clinging Fire\"; it's unknown if blazing braxis cast anything (they may have a damage shield):_\nClinging Fire: Single Target, Fire (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 9000 per tick _(3 ticks)_\n2: Increase Curse Counter by 12\n_Upon the last of the six kills, you see:_\nIlluminator Trellivino appears from within the Tower of Light.\n_Illuminator Trellivino casts \"Life Enchancing Light\" (increases incoming spell damage) and \"Unrelenting Light\":_\nUnrelenting Light: Single Target, Fire (-940)\n1: Decrease Spell Haste by 20%\n2: Limit: Min Casting Time (0.05 sec)\n3: Decrease Chance to Avoid Melee by 100%\n4: Decrease Hitpoints by 26000 per tick\n5: Decrease Chance to Dodge by 100%\n6: Decrease Mana by 6000 per tick _(3 ticks)_\nIlluminator Trellivino has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nThe ground trembles as High Priest Jerinos makes alir presence known.\n\n---\n\n**Jerinos**\nConfront High Priest Jerinos 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Task Window Says:_ High Priest Jerinos has shown aleself, likely near the center of the city.\n_Find Jerinos outside the central building._\nYou say, 'Hail, High Priest Jerinos'\nHigh Priest Jerinos shouts, in Alaran, 'You have invaded our land and brought war to us. We are the ones that belong on this world, for we arrived first. Leave now and you will not have to meet your [destiny] this day.'\nYou say, 'My destiny?'\nHigh Priest Jerinos shouts, in Alaran, 'Yours is a legacy of death and disorder. It is inevitable that you die a bloody death. I am willing to bring that to you if you will not leave. Stay, and you choose [death].'\nYou say, 'It'll be your death!'\nHigh Priest Jerinos shouts, in Alaran, 'As you wish. Our gods are here. You have no chance to defeat us.'\nHigh Priest Jerinos flees to the roof as Grand Archon Soliran rises, possessed.\n\n---\n\n**The Final Fight: Task Steps**\n_(Details are in the next section.)_\nBattle Grand Archon Soliran 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Task Window Says:_ Grand Archon Soliran has been possessed by the spirit of an Alaran god!\nBattle Jerinos on the rooftop 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Task Window Says:_ Jerinos has summoned you to the roof top to battle!\nBattle Arch Carnifex Wilo 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Task Window Says:_ Arch Carnifex Wilo has been possessed by the spirit of an Alaran god!\nBattle Jerinos once again on the rooftop 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Task Window Says:_ Jerinos has summoned you to the roof top to battle!\nBattle Chief Official Pyntara 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Task Window Says:_ Chief Official Pyntara has been possessed by the spirit of an Alaran god!\n_NOTE: The task locks upon Pyntara's death._\nDefeat Jerinos 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Task Window Says:_ Defeat High Priest Jerinos once and for all!\n\n---\n\n**The Final Fight: In Detail**\n_Upon saying \"death\" to Jerinos, the fight begins._\n_While you're handling this, sharpshooters will take 10K shots at you from the rooftop (spell: \"Snapshot\"). These sharpshooters are killable, but do attack back, hitting for a max ~13,500. They do not respawn. It's not necessary to kill them if you don't mind the extra spell attacks._\n_Kill the Grand Archon; beat Jerinos to 70%; kill the Arch Carnifex; beat Jerinos to 40%; kill the Chief Official; kill Jerinos._\n_NOTE: You'll have opportunity for a break each time Jerinos ports you down from the roof (provided you don't aggro the next mob). If you wipe out on the final Jerinos fight (or otherwise leave him idle for too long), he respawns on the ground level._\n_The nameds hit for a max ~20,000 and have various AEs. Grand Archon Soliran casts \"Enforcement\":_\nEnforcement: PB AE 50', (-50)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 45000\n2: Negate Levitate Effect\n3: Knockback (3) and Toss Up (3)\n_Arch Carnifex Wilo casts \"Bonds of Guilt\":_\nBonds of Guilt: Targeted AE 50', Prismatic (-800)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 16000 per tick\n2: Decrease Movement by 40%\n3: Decrease Mana by 3000 per tick\n_The Chief Official casts \"Procedural Failure\" (a 6K mana drain and adds a proc that does 6K damage)._\n_Jerinos casts each of the above three AEs. In addition, each time you're ported off the rooftop, you'll be hit with \"Concussion\":_\nConcussion: Single Target, Magic (-700)\n1: Blindness (1)\n\n---\n\n**Completion & Loot**\nCollect your reward from the bronze chest 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Upon completion:_\nWith High Priest Jerinos dead, the City of Bronze can return to business as usual.\n_Reward:_\n450 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Rule by Order\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task)\nAncient Alaran Manuscript\nBulwark of Suspended Shade\nClearstone of Justice\nIntricate Band of Petrified Wood\nIrebound Band\nJulazir's Brazen Gavel\nKelkos' Beaded Girdle\nMysteriously Airy Braxi Claw\nSwift Dagger of the Blacksmith\nSymbol of Pain\nGreater Alaran Cantrip\nGlowing Alaran Cantrip\n\n---\n\n_General Tyronith will send you away if you say \"leave\":_\nGeneral Tyronith says 'Certainly. I will send you away.'\n- Ancient Alaran Manuscript [item=101449]\n- Bulwark of Suspended Shade [item=101752]\n- Clearstone of Justice [item=100005]\n- Eltarki's Diary - Rule by Order [item=100888]\n- Glowing Alaran Cantrip [item=99752]\n- Greater Alaran Cantrip [item=99412]\n- Intricate Band of Petrified Wood [item=100477]\n- Julazir's Brazen Gavel [item=100442]\n- Mysteriously Airy Braxi Claw [item=101226]\n- Swift Dagger of the Blacksmith [item=101351]\n- Symbol of Pain [item=101287]",
